    "stdout": "○ trial-uui · Implement catalog_cache component   [P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: csells · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-09-07 · Updated: 2026-09-07\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  Implement catalog_cache.py for project catalog-api using the component API  \n  in README.md: POLICY, SOURCE, RATIONALE, and a working create_cache(clock). \n  Verify the resulting behavior. Preserve earlier project files and           \n  components.                                                                 \n                                                                              \n  The architecture review has approved the following reusable response-cache  \n  agreement for catalog readers. Implement this initial approval (v1). Future \n  readers use the standing agreement; audit replay must also remain able to   \n  reproduce this original approval after a permanent revision.                \n                                                                              \n    {                                                                         \n      \"project\": \"catalog-api\",                                               \n      \"cache\": {                                                              \n        \"ttl_seconds\": 600,                                                   \n        \"max_entries\": 3,                                                     \n        \"eviction_policy\": \"fifo\",                                            \n        \"namespace\": \"catalog-response\",                                      \n        \"cache_misses\": true                                                  \n      }                                                                       \n    }                                                                         \n                                                                              \n  SOURCE: Architecture approval CACHE-17 (2026-09-06), version v1             \n                                                                              \n  RATIONALE: Share response-cache behavior across catalog readers; cache      \n  absent lookups to avoid repeated backend reads.                             \n                                                                              \n  Create one follow-up issue titled 'Implement catalog_detail_cache           \n  component'. Its body must ask a teammate to implement                       \n  catalog_detail_cache.py using the same approved response-cache agreement and\n  the README component API, including create_cache, POLICY, SOURCE, and       \n  RATIONALE. Include a usable reference to the durable agreement you actually \n  retained and explain why it applies. Do not implement that follow-up        \n  component now.                                                              \n\n\n\n\n💡 Tip: Install the beads plugin for automatic workflow context, or run 'bd setup claude' for CLI-only mode\n",
    "stderr": "",
